      "message": "actually, how is this going to work for boards that provide their\nown udelay(). i only see zinger do this.\n\nif the common implementation is weak, then one of the non-weak\nimplementations under chip/... or core/host will prevail. we\nshould mark those as __override.\n\nbut, if a board provides its own override, like zinger does,\nit would collide with the udelay() defined in chip/....\nturns out, in the zinger case, there is no chip specific\nimplementation, so we\u0027ll get away with it.\n\nare you OK with accepting this hypothetical issue?",
